---
/**
 * Asking a client for their email, at the moment it is actually needed.
 *
 * Payment used to stop at "we need an email address on this quote, please get
 * in touch", which asks somebody holding their card to go and send an email
 * instead. The address is the only thing missing and they are the person who
 * has it, so ask them here and say why.
 *
 * A real `<dialog>`: focus trapping, Escape and an inert background come free,
 * and hand-rolling those is how a modal ends up trapping a keyboard user.
 * Styled entirely here, so it is ours rather than the browser's.
 *
 * Rendered only when there is no address on file. A dialog in the DOM that can
 * never open is a thing to trip over later.
 *
 * The script that drives it lives with the pay button in QuoteDocument, because
 * the two are one flow: ask, save, then continue to checkout.
 */
---

<dialog
  data-email-dialog
  aria-labelledby="email-dialog-title"
  class="m-auto w-[min(28rem,calc(100vw-2rem))] rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-6 text-foreground backdrop:bg-foreground/40 backdrop:backdrop-blur-sm md:p-8"
>
  <h2 id="email-dialog-title" class="font-display text-2xl leading-tight">
    Where should we send the receipt?
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-base text-muted-foreground">
    Paystack needs an email address to take the payment. We use it for your receipt, the invoice,
    and anything we need to ask you about this project. Nothing else, and no marketing.
  </p>

  <form data-email-form class="mt-5 flex flex-col gap-3" novalidate>
    <label class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
      <span class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Your email address</span>
      <input
        type="email"
        name="email"
        required
        autocomplete="email"
        inputmode="email"
        placeholder="you@company.com"
        data-email-input
        class="min-h-12 w-full rounded-xl border border-border bg-background px-4 text-base outline-none focus-visible:border-foreground"
      />
    </label>

    <p data-email-error class="hidden text-sm text-destructive" role="alert"></p>

    <div class="mt-2 flex flex-col-reverse gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:justify-end">
      <button
        type="button"
        data-email-cancel
        class="min-h-12 rounded-full border border-border px-6 text-base transition-colors hover:bg-muted"
      >
        Cancel
      </button>
      <button
        type="submit"
        data-email-submit
        class="min-h-12 rounded-full bg-accent px-6 text-base text-accent-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-foreground hover:text-background disabled:opacity-60"
      >
        Save and continue
      </button>
    </div>
  </form>
</dialog>
